<p> -State and Local		 813.9    811.4    807.7    804.3</p>
<p>A-Advance. P-Preliminary. F-Final.  </p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected the initial estimate of first quarter GDP to show a 4.1 percent rise, the price index to be up 2.1 percent and the implicit deflator to rise 1.7 percent.</p>
<p>Commerce provides three estimates of GDP per quarter. The first is the advance (A) estimate, the second is the preliminary (P) estimate, and the last is the final (F) estimate.</p>
<p>The department said the increase in GDP in the first quarter was the largest since a 6.0 percent rise in the fourth quarter of 1987.  </p>
<p>The rise in consumer outlays in the first quarter was the largest since a 7.2 percent increase in the first quarter of 1988.</p>
<p>The percentage jump in imports of goods and services last quarter was the biggest since a 35.9 percent surge in the first quarter of 1984.</p>
<p>The increase in the government's price index was the largest since a 3.3 percent rise in the first quarter of 1995.</p>
<p>The first quarter increase in the implicit price deflator was the largest since a 2.4 percent rise in the second quarter of 1995.</p>
